\begin{abstract}
Network intrusion detection systems require both high accuracy and interpretability for deployment in Security Operation Centers. We propose Vupr-QLI, a novel framework that maps statistical network-flow features into a complex coherence manifold $Q = x + iy$, where $x$ represents coherent transport dynamics and $y$ characterizes instability fluctuations. Evaluated on CIC-IDS2017 \cite{sharafaldin2018toward}, Vupr-QLI achieves 0.947 AUC for DoS Hulk detection with 91.2\% TPR at 7.1\% FPR, outperforming Random Forest \cite{breiman2001random} and recent deep models \cite{yang2023hierarchical,wang2024dual} while requiring no GPU training. The framework processes 120,000 flows/sec on a single CPU core, offering a lightweight, interpretable alternative to black-box IDS. Coherence magnitude and phase analysis provide direct diagnostics of attack behavior, enabling explainable security decisions.
\end{abstract}

